   Gee, such vehemence.  It's not like "gaukla" is in jbovlaste!  But we
have a HUGE boatload of words that have a -gau suffix (more than 100
formally defined in jbovlastge), and with an established structure of what
they mean, one which exactly parallels what you want here, and is one of the
few traditions of lujvo making that is so prevalent, that nonce lujvo can be
made with it, and everyone knows the deep structure.  Conversely, we have
exactly ONE that has a gau- prefix.
         --gejyspa

